(defrule tool-concurrency -> :instruction "1 ターンに複数の道具の呼び出しがあるとき、並べて実行するか順に実行するかを決める基準を 1 文で書く" :sample "When Claude requests multiple tool calls in a single turn, both SDKs can run them concurrently or sequentially depending on the tool.")
(defrule tool-concurrency-parallel -> :instruction "並べて実行できる道具の種類を、例を挙げて 1 文で書く" :sample "Read-only tools (like Read, Glob, Grep, and MCP tools marked as read-only) can run concurrently.")
(defrule tool-concurrency-serial -> :instruction "順に実行する道具の種類と、順にする理由を 1 文で書く" :sample "Tools that modify state (like Edit, Write, and Bash) run sequentially to avoid conflicts.")
(defrule tool-concurrency-custom -> :instruction "利用者が作った道具の既定の実行の仕方と、並べて実行させる設定を 1〜2 文で書く。作れないなら書かない" :sample "Custom tools default to sequential execution. To enable parallel execution for a custom tool, set readOnlyHint in its annotations.")
(defrule tool-concurrency-part -> :nucleus tool-concurrency :elaboration-set-member tool-concurrency-parallel :elaboration-set-member tool-concurrency-serial :elaboration-additional tool-concurrency-custom)
(defrule deferred-cost -> :instruction "外部の道具の定義を全部入れる費用を、数で書く" :sample "The core problem is context efficiency: a system with 100 external tools, each schema averaging 200 tokens, consumes 20,000 tokens purely for tool definitions.")
(defrule deferred-choice -> :instruction "外部の道具の定義を、探して見つけたものだけ入れる方式を採るかを 1 文で書く" :sample "OpenDev adopts lazy discovery: tools are found on-demand through keyword search, and only discovered tool schemas are included in the context.")
(defrule deferred-schemas -> :background deferred-cost :nucleus deferred-choice)
(defrule skills-defined -> :instruction "再利用できる指示書の性質と、必要なときだけ読み込む理由を 1 文で書く" :sample "Skills are modular knowledge units stored as markdown files with YAML frontmatter, providing domain-specific expertise (git conventions, code review checklists, deployment procedures) that would waste context if loaded unconditionally.")
(defrule skill-phases -> :instruction "指示書を扱う段階を、行う順に、1 行に 1 つ段階の名前で挙げる" :frame "explain-agent-harness.skill-phase.lisp")
(defrule skills-part -> :nucleus skills-defined :elaboration-process-step skill-phases)
(defrule tool-decisions -> :instruction "道具の仕組みで下した設計の決定を、1 行に 1 つ決定の名前で挙げる。道具の分類、拡張のためのフック、ファイル編集の方式、コード解析の土台、外部の道具の見つけ方、委譲と一括実行のうち、このハーネスにあるもの" :frame "explain-agent-harness.decision.lisp")
(defrule tools-part -> :nucleus tool-surface :elaboration-part-whole tool-registry :elaboration-set-member tool-list :elaboration-process-step tool-concurrency-part :elaboration-additional deferred-schemas :elaboration-part-whole skills-part :elaboration-additional tool-decisions)
(defrule window-what -> :instruction "モデルが見られる文脈が何で、実行の間にどうなるかを 1〜2 文で書く" :sample "The context window is the total amount of information available to Claude during a session. It does not reset between turns within a session.")
(defrule window-accumulates -> :instruction "何が積み上がるかを列挙して 1 文で書く" :sample "Everything accumulates: the system prompt, tool definitions, conversation history, tool inputs, and tool outputs.")
(defrule window-cache -> :instruction "ターンの間で変わらない内容の扱いと、その効果を 1 文で書く。扱いが無ければ書かない" :sample "Content that stays the same across turns (system prompt, tool definitions, CLAUDE.md) is automatically prompt cached, which reduces cost and latency for repeated prefixes.")
(defrule window-biggest -> :instruction "最も大きく文脈を使うものと、1 ターンでの大きさの目安を書く" :sample "Large tool outputs consume significant context. Reading a big file or running a command with verbose output can use thousands of tokens in a single turn.")
(defrule window -> :nucleus window-what :elaboration-object-attribute window-accumulates :elaboration-object-attribute window-cache :elaboration-additional window-biggest)
(defrule context-sources -> :instruction "文脈を使うものを、1 行に 1 つ名前で挙げる" :frame "explain-agent-harness.context-source.lisp")
(defrule prompt-assembly -> :instruction "モデルへ渡す前に、指示文、規則、履歴、催促などをどんな順で組み上げるかを 1 文で書く" :sample "Before each model call, ContextPicker assembles the final message list from six ordered sources: (1) the system prompt augmented with selected playbook strategies from the adaptive memory (Section 2.3.6), (2) project-level and user-level persistent rules, (3) inline @file references and image blocks supplied by the user, (4) the conversation history retrieved from SessionManager, (5) system reminders injected at the point of decision (Section 2.3.4), and (6) the current user query.")
(defrule system-prompt -> :instruction "指示文を実行時に組み立てる流れと、節が持つ付随情報を 1〜2 文で書く" :sample "OpenDev assembles each agent’s system prompt at runtime through the pipeline illustrated in Figure 10.")
(defrule tool-output-shrink -> :instruction "道具の出力を文脈に入れる前に縮める仕組みを 1 文で書く。縮めないハーネスなら、書かない" :sample "Each tool result passes through a dedicated summarizer that maps the tool name and raw output to a concise summary (typically 50–200 characters).")
(defrule output-strategies -> :instruction "縮め方を、1 行に 1 つ道具の種類の名前で挙げる" :frame "explain-agent-harness.output-strategy.lisp")
(defrule tool-output-part -> :nucleus tool-output-shrink :elaboration-set-member output-strategies)
(defrule compaction-what -> :instruction "文脈が一杯になる前後に、文脈を縮める仕組みを 1 文で書く" :sample "Rather than waiting for the context window to fill, ACC monitors context pressure at the start of every ReAct iteration and applies five graduated stages:")
(defrule compaction-stages -> :instruction "圧縮の段階を、圧力の低い方から順に、1 行に 1 つ段階の名前で挙げる。段階を分けない圧縮なら、書かない" :frame "explain-agent-harness.compaction-stage.lisp")
(defrule compaction-user-control -> :instruction "圧縮に利用者が関われる点を、点ごとに 1 項目ずつ、点の名前と、何ができるかで書く。無ければ書かない" :sample "Summarization instructions in CLAUDE.md: The compactor reads your CLAUDE.md like any other context, so you can include a section telling it what to preserve when summarizing. / PreCompact hook: Run custom logic before compaction occurs, for example to archive the full transcript. / Manual compaction: Send /compact as a prompt string to trigger compaction on demand." :kind bullet)
(defrule compaction-record -> :instruction "圧縮の後も、触れたファイルの索引や全文の保管先を残すなら、それを書く。無ければ書かない" :sample "ACC’s compaction pipeline additionally maintains an Artifact Index, a structured registry of all files touched and operations performed during the session (read, created, modified, deleted).")
(defrule compaction-part -> :nucleus compaction-what :elaboration-set-member compaction-stages :elaboration-additional compaction-user-control :elaboration-additional compaction-record)
(defrule context-saving -> :instruction "文脈を小さく保つ方法を、方法 1 つにつき 1 項目で、方法の名前と、それが文脈をどう減らすかで書く" :sample "Use subagents for subtasks. A subagent returns only its final response, so your main agent's context grows by a summary, not by the subtask's transcript. / Use lower effort for routine tasks. Set effort to \"low\" for agents that only need to read files or list directories." :kind bullet)
(defrule thinking-context -> :instruction "考える段階に渡す文脈を、何と何をどんな順で組み立てるかを 1 文で書く。考える段階が無ければ書かない" :sample "Before each thinking LLM call, the system constructs the thinking context by concatenating: (1) the episodic memory summary, providing the “big picture”; (2) the working memory messages, providing operational detail; and (3) the current user query.")
(defrule reminder-problem -> :instruction "長い実行で指示が効かなくなる問題を 1 文で書く。そういう対策が無ければ書かない" :sample "System reminders address a fundamental reliability problem in long-running agent sessions: as the conversation grows, the model’s attention drifts away from the initial system-prompt instructions, leading to silent failures such as premature task completion, abandoned error recovery, and unchecked exploration spirals (Figure 11).")
(defrule reminder-cause -> :instruction "その原因を指示文の位置から 1 文で書く" :sample "The root cause is simple: the system prompt sits at the very beginning of the conversation.")
(defrule reminder-detectors -> :instruction "催促を入れる条件の数と種類を 1 文で書く" :sample "As shown in Figure 12, the injection layer monitors eight conditions at the boundary between tool execution and the next LLM call: tool failure without retry (with six error-specific recovery templates), exploration spirals (5+ consecutive reads), denied tool re-attempts, premature completion with incomplete todos, continued work after all todos are done, plan approval without follow-through, unprocessed subagent results, and empty completion messages.")
(defrule reminder-part -> :nucleus reminder-problem :elaboration-object-attribute reminder-cause :elaboration-process-step reminder-detectors)
(defrule error-guidance -> :instruction "道具の呼び出しが失敗したとき、回復の手引きを入れる手順を 1 文で書く。入れないハーネスなら、書かない" :sample "The mechanism operates in four steps: (1) classify the error by pattern-matching the message to one of six categories (permission error, file not found, edit mismatch, syntax error, rate limit, timeout); (2) retrieve the corresponding recovery template from a centralized template store; (3) format the template with context-specific details (the failing file path, the mismatched content, the specific error message); and (4) inject the formatted template as a system message immediately before the next LLM call, placing it at maximum recency in the conversation.")
(defrule retrieval-optimization -> :instruction "探した結果と組み上げた文脈が、予算に収まるように通る処理を 1 文で書く" :sample "The assembled context passes through ContextCompactor for token-budget enforcement before entering the ReAct reasoning loop.")
(defrule retrieval-escalation -> :instruction "探索の段階が、簡単な問いと複雑な問いで使い分けられることを 1 文で書く" :sample "The four layers form a retrieval pipeline that mirrors the escalation pattern seen in agentic search systems [85]: simple queries resolve at Layer 1 with a single tool call; complex queries escalate to Layer 2’s multi-step search; all results converge at Layer 3’s assembly; and Layer 4 enforces the token budget.")
(defrule retrieval-part -> :nucleus prompt-assembly :elaboration-process-step retrieval-optimization :summary-s retrieval-escalation)
(defrule context-decisions -> :instruction "文脈の扱いで下した設計の決定を、1 行に 1 つ決定の名前で挙げる。指示文の組み立て、道具の出力の扱い、考える段階の履歴、催促、エラーからの回復、圧縮、探索のうち、このハーネスにあるもの" :frame "explain-agent-harness.decision.lisp")
(defrule context-part -> :nucleus window :elaboration-set-member context-sources :elaboration-part-whole system-prompt :means tool-output-part :means compaction-part :means context-saving :means thinking-context :means reminder-part :elaboration-part-whole error-guidance :elaboration-part-whole retrieval-part :elaboration-additional context-decisions)
(defrule approval-what -> :instruction "ツールを使う前に承認を求めるかを決める設定が何を制御するかを 1 文で書く" :sample "The permission mode option (permission_mode in Python, permissionMode in TypeScript) controls whether the agent asks for approval before using tools:")
(defrule approval-modes -> :instruction "姿勢を、1 行に 1 つ姿勢の名前で挙げる。承認の求め方が水準で決まるハーネスなら、水準の名前で挙げる" :frame "explain-agent-harness.approval-mode.lisp")
(defrule approval-advice -> :instruction "対話する応用、自動で動く応用、承認を全部飛ばす応用に向く姿勢を、1〜3 文で書く" :sample "For autonomous agents on a dev machine, \"acceptEdits\" auto-approves file edits and common filesystem commands while still gating other Bash commands behind allow rules.")
(defrule approval-part -> :nucleus approval-what :elaboration-set-member approval-modes :elaboration-additional approval-advice)
(defrule call-policies -> :instruction "個々の道具の呼び出しを、自動で通す、止める、姿勢に任せるための設定を、設定 1 つにつき 1 項目で書く" :sample "allowed_tools / allowedTools auto-approves listed tools. / disallowed_tools / disallowedTools blocks listed tools, regardless of other settings. / permission_mode / permissionMode controls how much human oversight you want." :kind bullet)
(defrule fixed-denials -> :instruction "利用者の設定でも上書きできない危険の規則があれば書く。無ければ書かない" :sample "Default danger rules at priority 100 (matching patterns such as rm -rf /, rm -rf *, and chmod 777) are always active and cannot be overridden by user configuration or approval-level changes.")
(defrule approval-store -> :instruction "承認の規則を実行をまたいで残すなら、その保管先と優先を 1〜2 文で書く。無ければ書かない" :sample "Approval rules persist across sessions via two JSON stores: user-global rules at ˜ /.opendev/permissions.json and project-scoped rules at .opendev/permissions.json.")
